<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n23288" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in-frĕmo</span></b> , ŭi,
		3, v. n., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to make</i> or <i>utter a noise</i>
				(<b>poet.</b>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, <i>to growl</i>, <i>bellow</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">infremuitque ferox, of the wild boar,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 10, 711</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, of things, <i>to
			roar</i>, <i>rage</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">bellum infremuit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sil.
					3, 230</span></i>
			. </div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
